  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "PeerSharp 5.4.0 leaves a session as it was across a restart. Renames, file selections and progress are now saved for stopped and never-started torrents, torrents waiting in the queue stay there, and ratio limits count earlier sessions. A paused session comes back paused, even with no torrents in it, and a start, stop, pause or resume is saved as it happens, so a crash straight after one no longer loses it. Stopping and starting a torrent after a restart no longer throws away pieces in files it had written to, and a file check no longer holds up the queue. Adds IClientEngine.SessionRestoredPaused and SavedSessionState. Needs Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions 10.0.14 or later. Binary compatible with 5.3.1. See https://github.com/ligenq/PeerSharp/blob/v5.4.0/CHANGELOG.md.",
